& [SourceIntegrity] passed at 12356 bytes SHA256 521A2E7A29B5D15E98F20A9D5A175BE31798618F7008C93812C45738D44FA4E5
& [Baseline] is pushed commit 2e504d74a109e85d7f4e5ed333016e1183cad77b
& [FormationAuthority] exists because residual identity and code-binding description are documentary and pure
& [ImplementationAuthority] is absent because I03C has no activation source signature active phase lock or registry module

& [Correction1] closes the stage vocabulary
  + byte_ingress deserialize semantic_validation preparation authorship authorship_replay coordination_replay tool_schema tool_call controller_verification controller_replay admission and bounded_execution
  + a record may name multiple ordered stages but cannot invent a free-text stage

& [Correction2] distinguishes covered roots from applicability
  + covered root states that the root can carry the relevant subject or condition
  + applicability is an exact predicate narrowing when the residual governs
  + all-roots coverage never means that every instance invokes the named authority

& [Correction3] closes code-binding identity
  + crate module function names and whole-source byte length plus SHA256 form the binding
  + current file path and line are advisory locators only
  + external bindings name package concept and locked dependency identity when available
  + a source digest change makes the binding stale even when a function retains its name

& [Correction4] separates enforcement from I03 evaluation
  + enforced partially_enforced unimplemented observational and outside_i03 describe current implementation state
  + safe_pure observational_only and prohibited_authority describe what an eventual I03 evaluator may do
  + neither field upgrades the other or grants execution authority

& [Correction5] narrows RMS-R01
  + serde_json recursion behavior is external implementation capacity rather than a public schema guarantee
  + the registry may observe the locked dependency and prove finite test behavior
  + it cannot claim a stable public recursion contract without an owned ingress and typed-reader boundary

& [Correction6] narrows RMS-R06
  + all five documents cite the universe residual family, so all five remain covered
  + applicability is only an artifact reaching Observer admission
  + evaluation is prohibited because I03 is conformance observation and may not execute admission authority

& [Correction7] splits I03-R020's dual character
  + zero provider and external-effect counters are enforceable result evidence
  + architectural non-capability is observational and cannot be inferred solely from counters
  + the closed enforcement disposition remains enforced because the bounded implementation lacks provider and effect facilities and verifies zero counters
  + its proof is conjunctive and requires both code-surface observation and result verification while its I03 policy remains observational_only

& [Correction8] closes proof-reference semantics
  + proof references are repository-relative artifact identities or named future proof obligations
  + existence proves only traceability
  + satisfaction requires the referenced proof family to assert the exact record condition under the bound source snapshot

& [Correction9] closes index semantics
  + records are authoritative and indexes are fully derived
  + every index value is a sorted unique residual-id vector
  + missing extra duplicated or differently ordered membership is a registry construction fault
  + stored indexes must equal independently reconstructed indexes byte for byte after canonical encoding

& [Correction10] closes schema-reference resolution
  + scan only each CanonicalMachineSchemaDocument residual_ids set in the exact I02 bundle payload documents map
  + the five standalone schema JSON payloads intentionally omit residual metadata and are never scanned for it
  + every encountered identifier resolves to exactly one record
  + every RMS-R01 through RMS-R06 record is cited and I03-R007 through I03-R020 remain registry-only until later documents cite them

& [Correction11] closes registry digest scope
  + domain profile parent I03 UUID exact I02 bundle digest ordered source snapshots ordered records and canonical derived indexes are bound
  + commentary line locators and filesystem timestamps are excluded

& [Correction12] corrects future feature wording
  + schema-conformance is a proposed future feature name only
  + activation must first prove it does not collide with existing Cargo feature policy
  + formation cannot modify Cargo metadata or reserve the feature by assertion

& [Correction13] closes I02 bundle identity
  + artifact identity is 247809 exact bytes with file SHA256 03616F46C4A3C4B7FA4B9D0A668E16FF4B47BA71CB70879B10F1D95157ADCB42
  + embedded payload digest is sha256 34f580f21825860ec03ed0bd089ab2b34ae8c08dd1d8cb66f22a629750314167
  + embedded exact-baseline fingerprint is sha256 77668e20c701723929cb9b12343ed33b21ee1f59da5ea121db3d0e0be94ba6d7
  + all three are bound because file identity payload semantic identity and generated baseline identity are distinct
  + none is represented as a digital signature

